[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/kit/issues/comments/968407367","html_url":"https://github.com/sveltejs/kit/issues/2802#issuecomment-968407367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/kit/issues/2802","id":968407367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEiPr8c45uLlH","user":{"login":"rmunn","id":90762,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn","html_url":"https://github.com/rmunn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-15T00:45:28Z","updated_at":"2021-11-15T00:45:28Z","body":"Changing the URL from `/#bug.html` to `/%23bug.html` lets the browser retrieve the file\\*. So the difference here is that Svelte-Kit's `fetch` can handle some characters that aren't URL-encoded. Whereas the browser's `fetch` treats that as retrieving the `/` URL with a hash of `bug.html`, and `/` maps to `/src/routes/index.html`.\r\n\r\n\\* I did have to edit the browser example as follows:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n    import { browser } from '$app/env';\r\n    async function loadBrowser() { /* ... */ }\r\n    if (browser) loadBrowser();\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat allows it to run *only* on the browser, instead of during server-side rendering. If I allowed the `loadBrowser` function from your reproduction to run during SSR, Node was throwing `TypeError [ERR_INVALID_URL]: Invalid URL` because the URL wasn't complete (no host, no protocol). (Svelte-Kit's `fetch` has an extra feature where you can write relative URLs and it will expand them based on the base URL you've specified in the config).\r\n\r\nIMHO this is a feature, not a bug, but I won't close this issue as I'd like to let a core team member weigh in in case they think this really is a bug.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/kit/issues/comments/968407367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rmunn","id":90762,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn","html_url":"https://github.com/rmunn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":5614996421,"node_id":"LE_lADOEiPr8c4-xKm8zwAAAAFOrgvF","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sveltejs/kit/issues/events/5614996421","actor":{"login":"rmunn","id":90762,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90762?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn","html_url":"https://github.com/rmunn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rmunn/followe